      <Docs>
        <param name="temporal">The temporal object to convert. It must not be <see langword="null" />.</param>
        <summary>Gets a zoned date-time from a temporal object.</summary>
        <returns>The converted zoned date-time, which is not <see langword="null" />.</returns>
        <remarks>
          <para>The conversion obtains the chronology, date, time, and time zone from <paramref name="temporal" />. It has the same behavior as calling <c>Chronology.zonedDateTime(TemporalAccessor)</c> on that chronology. A <see cref="T:Java.Time.DateTimeException" /> is thrown if the conversion cannot be completed.</para>
          <para>This legacy method exposes the Java static interface method. Use <see cref="M:Java.Time.Chrono.IChronoZonedDateTime.From(Java.Time.Temporal.ITemporalAccessor)" /> instead.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/java.base/java/time/chrono/ChronoZonedDateTime.html#from(java.time.temporal.TemporalAccessor)" title="Reference documentation">Java reference for <code>java.time.chrono.ChronoZonedDateTime.from</code>.</a></format></para>
        </remarks>
