      <Docs>
        <summary>Gets a comparator that orders zoned date-times by their instant, without comparing their calendar systems.</summary>
        <returns>A comparator that compares epoch seconds first, then nanoseconds within the second.</returns>
        <remarks>
          <para>The comparator compares only the instant. Date-times at the same instant compare as equal, even if their calendar systems differ. Unlike <see cref="M:Java.Time.Chrono.IChronoZonedDateTime.CompareTo(Java.Time.Chrono.IChronoZonedDateTime)" />, it does not use the local date-time, time-zone ID, or chronology to break a tie.</para>
          <para>This legacy method exposes the Java static interface method. Use <see cref="M:Java.Time.Chrono.IChronoZonedDateTime.TimeLineOrder" /> instead.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/java.base/java/time/chrono/ChronoZonedDateTime.html#timeLineOrder()" title="Reference documentation">Java reference for <code>java.time.chrono.ChronoZonedDateTime.timeLineOrder</code>.</a></format></para>
